From: David Bau <davidbau@csail.mit.edu>
Date: 2026-06-19
Subject: [PATCH] make_glib: mark disp.botl dirty on transition, not no-transition

`make_glib()` writes the wrong half of the "Slippery state changed?"
expression: `disp.botl |= (!Glib ^ !!xtime)`.  The intended idiom is
`(was_Slippery) ^ (will_be_Slippery)`, where each side is the
boolean coercion of a `long`.  Coerce-to-bool is `!!`; the existing
code uses `!` on the left half.  Truth-tabling all four
(old, new) state pairs confirms the expression returns the
*inverse* of the real boolean transition — it marks `disp.botl`
dirty exactly when Slippery does NOT change, and leaves it clean
when Slippery does change.

Self-correcting in normal play: `bot()` runs every turn driven by
other status changes that correctly mark `disp.botl`.  The
visible symptom is at most a one-turn lag in `Slippery` appearing
on or leaving the status line, and only when no other status
change happens in the same turn as the Glib transition.

Direct evidence the intended idiom is `!!`, not `!`: the sibling
function `make_deaf` at `potion.c:443-456`, twelve lines above
`make_glib`, writes exactly the same boolean-transition
predicate, but spelled in the more verbose form that elides the
typo risk:

    set_itimeout(&HDeaf, xtime);
    if ((xtime != 0L) ^ (old != 0L)) {
        disp.botl = TRUE;
        ...
    }

`(x != 0L) ^ (old != 0L)` is mathematically identical to
`(!!Glib) ^ (!!xtime)`.  The author of `make_glib` clearly knew
the right pattern; it's just a missed `!` keystroke.

Fix: insert the missing `!` so the left half is also a coerced
boolean.

---
 src/potion.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/potion.c b/src/potion.c
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/src/potion.c
+++ b/src/potion.c
@@ -460,7 +460,7 @@ make_glib(int xtime)
 void
 make_glib(int xtime)
 {
-    disp.botl |= (!Glib ^ !!xtime);
+    disp.botl |= (!!Glib ^ !!xtime);
     set_itimeout(&Glib, xtime);
     /* may change "(being worn)" to "(being worn; slippery)" or vice versa */
     if (uarmg)
